Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; Stained Glass OS -- Terminal (sg-terminal), Windows Terminal's stand-in.
; wt.exe from the Run box, ShellExecute and scripts opens it (wine-sg's
; system32 wt.exe hands off to this App Paths entry, so programs that
; CreateProcess wt.exe get it too), as does explorer's Win+X > Terminal.
;
; The path is the package's install location reached through Z:. If Z: is ever
; removed from the prefix for isolation, this must move with it.

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\App Paths\wt.exe]
@="Z:\\usr\\libexec\\stained-glass\\shell\\sg-terminal64.exe"
